# restic --exclude-file, wired into backup.sh's home snapshot.
#
# ADDITIVE. The inline --exclude flags in backup.sh still do the work for ~/.cache,
# which carries no CACHEDIR.TAG of its own (only 4 of its ~70 subdirs do) and is
# therefore NOT covered by --exclude-caches. Do not delete those inline flags.
#
# Syntax notes, both learned the hard way:
#   - A line is a comment only if it STARTS with '#'. A trailing comment becomes part
#     of the pattern and silently matches nothing.
#   - Patterns go through os.Expand: $HOME is expanded (so this file survives a new
#     username or home path), and a literal '$' must be written '$$'.
#
# Not listed here on purpose:
#   ~/.cache, ~/.npm/_cacache, ~/.cargo/registry, ~/.cargo/git
#       already excluded (inline flag / valid CACHEDIR.TAG)
#   ~/Dropbox
#       the daemon has been dead since 2025-05-07, so this is the ONLY copy of
#       keepass.kdbx. It must stay in the backup.
#   ~/.zsh_history
#       99k irreplaceable entries. The repo passphrase in it is fixed by rotating
#       the key, not by dropping the file.
#   ~/.beru/beru.db
#       live data, not cache. Excluding it silently would mean no backup at all.

# --- Provably derivable (the owning project says so) ---
# beru's SPEC: tokens.db is a cache over the raw archive, "rm tokens.db is a supported
# recovery". It is also a live WAL database being backfilled, so a copy would be torn.
# NOT the rest of ~/.beru/index: index/raw/<date>/*.ndjson (~555k files) is beru's
# authoritative, lossless archive — the source of truth everything else is rebuilt from.
$HOME/.beru/index/raw/tokens.db*

# --- Regenerable toolchain state (reinstalled by update.sh / the package manager) ---
# Checked: .pyenv holds only built interpreters (no virtualenvs), .nvm only node +
# npm/corepack/playwright, go/pkg/mod is Go's module cache, .debug is perf's
# build-id cache.
$HOME/.rustup
$HOME/go/pkg/mod
$HOME/.pyenv
$HOME/.nvm
$HOME/.debug

# --- This toolchain's own scratch ---
# ~/.dot/restore is restore.sh's staging dir. Backing it up means snapshotting a
# copy of a previous snapshot, and it has held root-owned /etc trees that made the
# next home backup fail with permission errors.
$HOME/.dot/restore
$HOME/.dot/logs

# --- Deliberately NOT excluded: large, but possibly the only copy. Your call. ---
# Each of these was once listed above as "derived" or "dead" on the strength of its
# name, and each turned out to be something else. Uncomment only what you have
# checked yourself.
#
#   65 GB  $HOME/.beru/index/raw/vectors.lmdb
#          beru's retired dense index, kept on purpose as a rollback target
#          (README: "temporary — expect a follow-up that drops both").
#   99 GB  $HOME/.beru/backups
#   47 GB  $HOME/.beru/beru.db.m5-preindex-bak
#          pre-migration copies of beru.db taken 2026-04-22.
#          $HOME/.beru/claude-mirror  — NEVER: the only surviving copy of ~72% of
#          your Claude Code transcripts (Claude Code deletes originals after 30 days).
#          $HOME/.mozilla/_firefox-cleanup-*  — the safety copy firefox/cleanup.sh
#          takes before it modifies profiles.
#          $HOME/Desktop/Old Firefox Data  — Firefox's pre-Refresh profile backup.
